All 258 tests pass. 

The change is complete. In `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, an owner creation is now rejected with **409 Conflict** when another owner already has the same last name and telephone number.

The implementation was localized to the existing `ownerAlreadyExists` helper in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:122`, which I narrowed from a full-field exact-duplicate match to matching solely on **last name + telephone**:

```java
private boolean ownerAlreadyExists(Owner owner) {
    return this.clinicService.findOwnerByLastName(owner.getLastName()).stream()
        .anyMatch(existing ->
            Objects.equals(existing.getLastName(), owner.getLastName())
                && Objects.equals(existing.getTelephone(), owner.getTelephone()));
}
```

The `addOwner` method already returns `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` when this returns true. The V2 controller only exposes paginated listing (no creation), so no change was needed there. Full suite is green (258 tests).
